// v0.119.0 -- the propensity subsystem on APO/APOS, checked against the
// REAL upstream implementation.
//
// # What this closes, and a correction
//
// Earlier v0.11x CHANGELOG entries named "ps_dm / the DR-learner" as the
// missing propensity-analysis subsystem. **That is wrong for
// doubleml 0.11.4**: `ps_dm` does not exist in this release. Reading
// the published sdist (`_verify/doubleml-0.11.4.tar.gz`) shows the
// subsystem is:
//
//   utils/_propensity_score.py
//       _normalize_ipw(propensity_score, treatment_indicator)
//       _propensity_score_adjustment(ps, d, normalize_ipw)
//       _trimm(preds, trimming_rule, trimming_threshold)
//   utils/propensity_score_processing.py
//       PSProcessor / PSProcessorConfig  (clip + optional isotonic)
//
// And this port ALREADY HAS `PSProcessor` -- config, clipping, PAVA
// isotonic calibration, CV calibration, all of it, exported. The claim
// that it had "no counterpart" was as wrong as the `ps_dm` one.
//
// What is genuinely missing is narrower and is what this round ports:
//
//   1. `normalize_ipw` / `propensity_score_adjustment` / `trim_predictions`
//      as PUBLIC, shared functions. `cvar.mbt` had carried a PRIVATE copy
//      of `_normalize_ipw` since its own `normalize_ipw` option landed,
//      so the formula existed twice in one package and neither copy
//      could be checked against upstream.
//   2. The `normalize_ipw` constructor flag on `DoubleMLAPO` and
//      `DoubleMLAPOS`, which upstream has (`apo.py:97`) and this port
//      did not -- so `E[Y(t)]` here could not be computed with
//      normalized inverse-probability weights at all.
//
// # The oracle
//
// `_verify/gen_v119_oracle.py` imports upstream's own functions from the
// published sdist and calls them. Every constant below is copied from
// `_v119_golden.json`; nothing is transcribed by hand. The port's DGP
// uses the same `np.random.default_rng(3141)` draw as the oracle's
// NumPy side, regenerated from the index in MoonBit.
//
// MEASURED on that fixture (`n = 200`):
//
//   mean_treat1 = 0.8813990350530895
//   mean_treat0 = 1.114904578741986
//   adjust_ps(identity) max diff = 0.0        <- normalize_ipw=False is exact
//   adjust_ps doctest  -> [0.01, 0.2, 0.5, 0.8, 0.99]
//   rows clipped on the real fixture = 0 of 200

///|
fn v119_dgp() -> (Array[Double], Array[Double]) {
  (v119_fixture_ps(), v119_fixture_d())
}

